# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale da
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [05:00, 10:00).
#
# Resolved by native review (docs/languages/da.md, "Open questions").
# Only the DEFINITE form ships here, deliberately excluding the bare
# "morgen" that sibling dayparts (aften/aftenen, nat/natten) both ship --
# bare "morgen" is the relative-day word for "tomorrow" ("i morgen"), and
# registering it as a daypart surface too would collide with that reading
# on every sentence. "morgenen" never appears in the tomorrow idiom ("i
# morgen" is always the bare form), so it carries no such ambiguity. The
# same surface is already used safely as a meridiem marker in
# clock_meridiem_am.voc ("klokken ni om morgenen" == 09:00).
morgenen